        "id": 1015428
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-03-20T07:29:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You still have two separate calls. It\u0027s now fine in terms of call stacks (where and when it\u0027s called) but there are still severe readability problems – namely, this will be called when you call `getKeepaliveDelaySeconds` (you do not expect a getter to do side effects) and also when you call `areLongLivedTcpConnectionsExpensive` without arguments (which is all the more confusing as there is a version that takes an argument) which is a landmine.\n\nYou\u0027re getting close – I would advise just removing completely the `areLongLivedTcpConnectionsExpensive` version without arguments, and calling getKeepaliveDelaySeconds directly in agentConnect instead.",
      "parentUuid": "b8104d16_8f1d0294",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3498,
        "startChar": 40,
        "endLine": 3498,
        "endChar": 73
      },
